{
  "name": "claudeconnect",
  "version": "2.7.1",
  "released": "2026-10-14",
  "notes": [
    "No more claim step in setup. Once Cloudflare Access is on, setup opens your site by itself: sign in with your email and it's yours. The Open button at the end does the same.",
    "Behind the scenes, that first visit still carries a one-time code. That's how your site knows the Access sign-in is yours, so a sign-in from anyone else's Cloudflare account is never trusted, even before Access is on or if it's ever turned off.",
    "The last setup screen says your site's own name (\"Open ChatGPT\") instead of ClaudeConnect.",
    "If you open the site before that first visit, it says it's almost ready and how to finish, in plain words."
  ],
